# The two wrapper launchers, each with the line endings its interpreter needs.
#
# cmd.exe reads a batch file line by line as it executes it, so a gradlew.bat normalised to LF
# is a build that fails on Windows for a reason nothing in the output names. The shell script is
# pinned the other way for the same reason: a clone on a Windows checkout with autocrlf would
# otherwise hand /bin/sh a file whose first line ends in a carriage return.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git neither normalises it nor tries to diff it.
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
